+  // event listener, which JavaScript reports instead of passing on): written
+  // on the standard error, as the server thread does, rather than ending the
+  // process (Node) or the run (the page sees a worker's uncaught errors).
+  // Under Node only on the main thread: a pthread's process.exit() ends just
+  // that thread, and the error must reach the main thread (Emscripten passes
+  // it on) so that the process ends with a non-zero status, e.g. after
+  // Interpreter::logicError() traps
